From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] comdlg32: Windows 7's item dialog in the Windows 7 shell

Purpose: the file and folder dialogs (IFileDialog) of the Windows 7 shell's
session look and work as Windows 7's: the taskbar's New toolbar, Browse
buttons, and applications' Open and Save dialogs.
Windows behavior (reference machine, Windows 7 Basic, 96 dpi): the dialog is
640x478 with no Help button in the caption. Its top row (35 high, the
visual style's Navbar::Rebar background) has Back and Forward (Navigation)
with the recent places' arrow, the address as a breadcrumb (the current
folder's icon, then each folder with an arrow that lists its folders; an
edit box when the empty part is clicked; AddressBand frame, BreadcrumbBar
split buttons, Go::Toolbar drop-down and Refresh), and the search box
("<folder>の検索" in italics, grey, on the inside of the SearchBox frame, magnifier). The browser fills the width
below it, without the details and preview panes (nor their buttons). At
the bottom: the name box (27 high, its label ending at 193) and the buttons
(30 high, at least 86 wide, 15 apart, 17 from the right and 14 from the
bottom), the size grip, all in the message font. With FOS_PICKFOLDERS the
label is "Folder:" and the button "Select Folder". The first folder is the
Documents library.
Wine before: Wine's dialog (440x300 dialog units, MS Shell Dlg 8, Help
button), an empty top row (its toolbar's bitmaps did not show), "File
name:" and "Open" for folders, the details pane, the desktop first.
Change: when WIN4WINE_SHELL is win7, the dialog makes those changes. The
top row is a new control (navbar7.c) drawn with the visual style's parts
(measured from the parts Windows 7's own navigation bar draws, traced with
+uxtheme) and explorerframe.dll's bitmaps (Refresh and Go, the magnifier,
the clear button) and strings ("%1の検索", the address not found). It keeps
its own recent places, navigates the explorer browser, and filters the
folder's items by name through the browser's IFolderFilterSite (Windows 7
searches the index, which the prefix does not have). The panes are hidden
through SID_ExplorerPaneVisibility. The first folder is the Documents
folder: the library's view needs Windows Search's folder (SearchFolder.dll).
Evidence: the taskbar's New toolbar in the Wayland session compared with the
reference machine's: the same layout at the same size; the breadcrumb's
menus, typed paths with %APPDATA%, Back, Forward, Refresh and the search
filter work; an application's Open dialog with file types is laid out the
same way. Windows 7's own comdlg32 was tried in the shell process and
left: it needs ShellStyle.dll and Windows Search's components, and stops
in its view callbacks.
Scope: WIN4WINE_SHELL=win7 only; the XP and ReactOS sessions and Wine's
programs keep Wine's dialog.
